.TH ARES_REINIT_RAND 3 "15 November 2026"
.SH NAME
ares_reinit_rand \- Discard a channel's cached random bytes and reinitialize
its random source.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ares.h>

ares_status_t ares_reinit_rand(ares_channel_t *\fIchannel\fP)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A channel keeps a cache of random bytes from which DNS query ids, DNS 0x20
case randomization and DNS cookies are drawn.  A process whose address space is
cloned without a fork, as when a virtual machine is restored several times from
one snapshot or a process is restored from a checkpoint, holds the same cache in
every copy, so every copy sends the same query ids until the cache is used up.

\fBares_reinit_rand(3)\fP discards the cache and reinitializes the channel's
random source, so that the next query draws fresh bytes.  Call it after the
process has learned of such a restore, before its next query.  On Linux the
VMClock page (\fI/dev/vmclock0\fP, \fIlinux/vmclock-abi.h\fP) carries a
\fIvm_generation_counter\fP that the hypervisor changes on every restore.

The channel is locked for the duration of the call.
.SH RETURN VALUES
.TP 14
.B ARES_SUCCESS
The cache was discarded.
.TP 14
.B ARES_EFORMERR
\fIchannel\fP was NULL.
.SH AVAILABILITY
This function was first introduced in c-ares version 1.35.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ares_reinit (3),
.BR ares_init_options (3)
